cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 6-DOF Ballistic Model
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite both the
  software and the thesis it was developed for.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "de Padua Sanches"
    given-names: "Luiz Guilherme"
    affiliation: "Instituto de Matemática e Estatística, Universidade de São Paulo (IME-USP)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OAfundador/6-DOF-ballistic-model"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Six-degree-of-freedom exterior ballistics model for spin-stabilised
  projectiles, following McCoy's formulation, with optional layers for
  anti-air fragment lethality and Monte Carlo dispersion analysis.
  Developed for an undergraduate thesis in Applied and Computational
  Mathematics at IME-USP. The thesis itself was produced with the
  single-file engine preserved on the `legacy` branch; the `main` branch
  is a later refactor into a package, machine-verified to be bit-identical
  to it. Please state which branch you used.
keywords:
  - exterior ballistics
  - six degrees of freedom
  - rigid body dynamics
  - Monte Carlo
  - naval artillery
  - air defence
version: "2.0.0"
references:
  - type: book
    title: >-
      Modern Exterior Ballistics: The Launch and Flight Dynamics of
      Symmetric Projectiles
    authors:
      - family-names: McCoy
        given-names: Robert L.
    edition: "2nd"
    publisher:
      name: Schiffer Publishing
    year: 2012
